{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>A Sabbath to YHWH your Elohim.</b> It is entirely for HaShem — to learn and to teach, to observe and to do, and to delight in it according to the service due to His honor, may He be blessed, as in the saying: חַמְרָא וְרֵיחָנֵי פַּקְּחוּנִי (Ḥullin 13a?)." "<b>You and your son and your daughter.</b> The minors who act with their father's knowledge."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "The Aramaic phrase חמרא וריחני פקחוני (wine and spices restored my awareness) is cited by Sforno with the reference הוריות יג: (Horayot 13a/b), where the Sages describe how wine and fragrant spices revive the spirit. I have left the Hebrew/Aramaic quotation untranslated as per convention."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:31.629571051Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}